Grounding two claims before I write the list — what the project's own blueprint says about payments, and the current PH gateway landscape:

Everything's grounded now — code evidence plus the project's own production spec. Here are the must-do ideas, grouped and prioritized, each with the evidence that makes it "must" rather than "nice":

🔒 Security & privacy (do before anyone real uses this)
Security headers are missing. next.config.ts sets only poweredByHeader: false — no Content-Security-Policy, Strict-Transport-Security, X-Frame-Options/frame-ancestors, Referrer-Policy, or Permissions-Policy. One headers() block fixes clickjacking, MIME sniffing, and the biggest XSS blast radius. Effort: under an hour. This is the cheapest security win in the repo.
Right-to-delete doesn't exist. There's /api/account/export but no deletion route anywhere under app/api/account — yet the PH Data Privacy Act and both app stores require account+data deletion, and PRODUCTION_SPECIFICATION_V3.md already commits to redaction rules. Build DELETE /api/account (soft-delete → scheduled purge, sign out all sessions, keep only what disputes legally require). Effort: a day; blocker for launch gates.
Rate limits are process-local. rate-limit.ts keeps buckets in an in-memory Map — restarts and any second instance reset every window to empty. Fine for the demo; a hard blocker the day you run two processes. Move to the durable store when the DB lands (idea 6). Effort: half a day after the DB.
ServMate identity verification. Trust chips exist, but the person doing the wiring in your user's home is unverified. A KYC provider (selfie + PH ID check, e.g. Veriff/Sumsub class) behind an identity_verified flag is the single strongest safety feature for this marketplace — and it powers the "Verified" badge to mean something. Effort: days + provider cost; needs research when you pick one.
💸 Money (the product's biggest unlock)
PayMongo for GCash + cards — behind the abstraction your own spec demands. Today "pay after the job is done" is cash-only, which caps order value and gives the platform zero take-rate. The blueprint already dictates the shape: PaymentIntent lifecycle CREATED → PENDING_PROVIDER → SUCCEEDED | FAILED | EXPIRED, signed webhooks, idempotency keys, provider_webhook_events, no escrow claims until legal/provider confirmation (PRODUCTION_SPECIFICATION_V3.md §69, §175, §192). PayMongo fits: PaymentIntent API, GCash + cards, checkout_session.payment.paid webhooks, refunds/disputes endpoints (docs: payment-acceptance-key-concepts, Payments API PH). Effort: 1–2 weeks for a pay-on-booking flow; honest model is "pay when booked, refund via dispute," since GCash has no card-style preauth hold.
The file store is at its ceiling. .data/servem.json is one 336KB JSON file with no transactions, no write concurrency safety, and no backups. Your database-design.md already designs the schema — migrate to SQLite/Postgres with migrations before real users, and the rate-limit/session problems solve themselves. Effort: the week that pays for itself most.
⚡ Functions & reliability
Turn on the email that's already written. email.ts already speaks Resend's HTTP API — the code is done, the transport isn't. Get a key + sending domain, and password resets/booking notices stop being dev-console fiction. (Gravity also suggests Knock as a multi-channel orchestration layer — worth revisiting when SMS/push arrive, but activating Resend first is the MVP move since it's wired.) Effort: an hour plus DNS.
Realtime messaging/notifications. Zero setInterval/polling exists in the app tree — messages and the bell refresh only on navigation. Even cheap focus-based router.refresh() polling would stop the "did they reply?" problem; SSE later. Effort: hours (polling) → days (SSE).
CI enforcement. PIPELINE_POLICY.md exists but the 218-check e2e + 120 unit tests run only when someone remembers locally. Wire tsc && test && build && e2e into CI so the suite you already have actually gates merges. Effort: an afternoon.
🎨 Design & product
Search-as-mode (from the brainstorm): overlay combobox on the top-bar field, URL-synced, deleting the is-search-view/≤860 field-swapping. Makes search available on every phone screen, not just home.
Saved → shortlist. The save toggle now exists on cards; make Saved a real comparison surface (2–4 cards side by side, price/rating/replies rows) — the natural "which one do I pick?" moment Shopee users bring with them.
PWA install + offline shell. PH traffic is mobile-first and data-conscious; an installable app with a cached shell is distribution without an app store.
If I had to pick the two that matter most: headers (1) — 45 minutes, protects everything — and the DB migration (6) — everything else on this list gets harder on a JSON file.

